\f0\fs48\b\cf1 SiliconForest desktop\b0\cf0\par
\fs24 The desk is a Wayland session on an M1. \i chonkstep-darwin-desktop\i0 composites the windows. The dock is \i chonkstep-dock\i0. Apps stay unmodified: shims sit in front of them and never write into the bundle.\par
\fs32\b\cf3 What is on the machine\b0\cf0\par
\fs24\pard\li360
\bullet  \b Compositor.\b0  Themes, wallpaper, and window decorations come from Chonkstep itself.\par
\bullet  \b Dock.\b0  Pins for Terminal, Activity Monitor, Firefox, Preview, and the apps under test.\par
\bullet  \b Unmodified Apple apps.\b0  TextEdit 1.20, Preview, and Terminal 2.15 run from their own binaries.\par
\pard\li0\fs32\b\cf2 Layers\b0\cf0\par
\fs22\f1
compositor    chonkstep    decorations and themes\par
dock          pins         launch by bundle id\par
overlay       AppKit front TextEdit-only shims\par
app           TextEdit     SHA-256 checked every run\par
\f0\fs24\cf4 The overlay is a different install name, so dyld does not fold it onto the dock's AppKit.\cf0\par
}
